{
  "id": "r04",
  "text": "At the end, the view opens onto a street. A figure walks away from the camera. Names start appearing, and the face finally turns into view: Norman Reedus. Then comes Silent Hills. The anonymous experiment is connected to Hideo Kojima, Guillermo del Toro, and a series people already know. The reveal works because it arrives after the experience. You aren't being asked to imagine whether these people could make something frightening. You've just played the sales pitch. In an official KONAMI message, del Toro talks about working with Kojima on the teaser and the ideas they were exchanging. That made the collaboration feel tangible, even though the larger game remained a promise. And the ending itself draws a boundary we need to keep: the playable teaser says it has no direct relation to the main title. This corridor wasn't proof that a finished Silent Hills existed somewhere. P.T. was the real thing people had played. Silent Hills was the future they were imagining from it.",
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
